        "acceptedPr": null,
        "calls": 1,
        "title": "SDK final refusals now include free mode rate limits",
        "summary": "The SDK model provider in sdk/src/impl/model-provider.ts now treats a 429 response with the error code free_mode_rate_limited as a final, non-retryable refusal when the Retry-After header is 60 seconds or more. This prevents the AI SDK from ignoring the long wait and retrying on its own 2-8 second backoff, which previously caused a Desktop or Cloud model start to refund the purchase and surface a misleading session superseded 409 error instead of the rate limit message. The change adds a conditional when predicate to the final refusal matcher that checks the server's Retry-After value against AI_SDK_MAX_HONOURED_RETRY_AFTER_MS; shorter waits are still retried by the AI SDK as before. A new test file verifies that a daily-window refusal is refused once, keeps the server's copy, and never reaches the refunded-start 409.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "sdk/src/impl/model-provider.ts adds a fourth entry to FINAL_REFUSALS for 'free_mode_rate_limited' (429) with a when predicate that returns true only when retryAfterMsOf(response) >= AI_SDK_MAX_HONOURED_RETRY_AFTER_MS (60_000); the new test file sdk/src/impl/__tests__/free-mode-rate-limit-no-retry.test.ts asserts that a daily-window refusal is refused once and never reaches the refunded-start 409.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
